rea, has kept pace financially, holding more cash on hand than Spartz despite raising less overall.\n\nRaters across the spectrum put the race at Likely R or better for Republicans, and prediction markets price Ford's chances around 15 percent. A single Democratic-sponsored July poll showed a two-point race, but its age and sponsor warrant caution. The combination of district lean, incumbency, and a favorable Republican environment makes Spartz the clear favorite, with Ford needing a substantial late shift to contend.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1386, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1359, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1346, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1196, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1263, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1331, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1305, "margin": -8.0}]}